WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Welcome to part two of First Time Homebuyer Series.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.240
In this episode, we're gonna be going over negotiations.

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.960
So here we are, you found the house you like,

4
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.960
and now it's go time.

5
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.720
It's time for your realtor to sit down with you,

6
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.400
do a comparable market analysis,

7
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.800
and show you similar properties that closed

8
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.360
so you don't overpay.

9
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.080
So after your realtor does the comparable market analysis

10
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.680
for you, you should have the market value

11
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.760
of the property.

12
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.480
I recommend offering anywhere between five and 7%

13
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.760
below the market value, not the list price,

14
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.820
below the market value of the property.

15
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.700
Anything below five to 7% of the market value

16
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.140
is considered disrespectful

17
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.860
and you might turn off the seller to offer completely.

18
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.540
List price is what the seller thinks this property is worth,

19
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.260
market value is what it's actually worth.

20
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.900
There's one more opportunity you have to renegotiate

21
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.420
and that's when the appraisal comes in.

22
00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.380
If it's lower than what you offer,

23
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.940
you might be able to bring the seller down a little.

24
